{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q648591","formula":"CHP","hill":"CHP","elements":["H","C","P"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":1.0,"P":1.0},"names":{"en":"Methylidynephosphane","ru":"Метилидинфосфан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Methylidynephosphane (phosphaethyne) is a chemical compound with the chemical formula HC≡P. It was the first phosphaalkyne compound discovered, containing the unusual C≡P carbon-phosphorus triple bond. Although isolated samples of methylidynephosphane are impractical, other derivatives have been well studied such as tert-butylphosphaacetylene. The conjugate base of methylidynephosphane is cyaphide.","ru":"Метилидинфосфан (фосфоэтин) — химическое соединение, аналог цианистого водорода где вместо азота фосфор, химическая формула HCP. Это было первое открытое фосфоалкиновое соединение, содержащее необычную тройную связь углерод-фосфор C≡P. Хотя изолированные образцы метилидинфосфана непрактичны, другие производные, такие как трет-бутилфосфаацетилен, хорошо изучены. В основе метилидинфосфана лежит циафид."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":138843,"mass":43.992,"charge":0,"smiles":"C#P","inchikey":"DPYPSJGRRFKXBE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methylidynephosphane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"138843","atoms":3,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.743,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"P"},{"x":0.743,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.808,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,3],[1,2,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q648591","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methylidynephosphane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9C%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%84%